Actually, if you're willing to "be a wuss" (as you describe it), dealing
with clusters of ants isn't that bad.  I agree (and I expect David does
too) that it's easier to handle them from a hallway or other cinch
point, but if you just macro E-  Elbereth and lean on that key hard,
none of them will ever be able to hit you, and being surrounded might
actually make it easier to hit them, melee or otherwise, since they would
approach you all at once. (I once killed eight water demons this way;
&%^%*& quaffers and their bonesfiles.) And mumakil can always be outrun;
however I'm not sure that evading a mumak is not always particularly
dangerous, as it can be deadly if there's someone else you don't want
to meet on the other end of the hallway, or what have you.

Fortunately, mumakil are slow and respect Elbereth, so you can get three
or four squares away and be almost guaranteed of success before it gets
to you; and if it is next to you and you look down and failed, run away
some and do it again. Throwing daggers at it and recovering them safely
takes some tactical finesse, but it's nothing a serious NetHacker can't
learn.  I don't think David is trying to make people YASD; of course,
you will die when trying any new strategy, melee-focused or not, but
